# What a guardian says when Ada keeps hitting it after it fell: every spell after the knockout
# still lands (and was paid for). Line n of a guardian's node answers the n-th extra hit; past
# the last line, the last one repeats. grimoire_overkill follows once, after the pleading.
# A guardian without its own node uses "mercy" (narration). {foe} is the guardian's name.
# Draft lines (prompt 03 format); the real writing is prompt 07. See docs/WRITING.md.

== slime_mercy ==
Asterisk Slime: {shake}Blub!{/shake} I'm already a puddle!
Asterisk Slime: Stop! I yield! I'm just goo now!
Asterisk Slime: Mercy, little witch! There is nothing left to hit!
Asterisk Slime: ...why are you still casting at a puddle?

== knight_mercy ==
Sir Wherewell: Hold! I am down, witch. I yield!
Sir Wherewell: {shake}I yield, I said!{/shake} Have you no honour?
Sir Wherewell: Mercy! A knight on the floor is not a target!
Sir Wherewell: ...is this what you call relevance?

== mercy ==
: {foe} is already down, and begs for mercy.
: {foe} waves a tiny white flag.
: {foe} has nothing left to lose. Literally.

== grimoire_overkill ==
Grimoire: Every spell after the first was paid for, and hit a fallen foe. {rune LIMIT} 1 would have been kinder, and cheaper.
